# Styling Conventions

## Architecture

Styles are split across co-located CSS files under `src/styles/`. `src/index.css` is the entry point and contains only three things: `@import` statements, `@theme` design tokens, and `@layer base` resets.

```
src/
  index.css                    ← imports, tokens, base resets
  styles/
    typography.css             ← @utility type scale (type-display, type-title, etc.)
    shared.css                 ← reusable component classes (content-column, text-card, section-title)
    layout/
      header.css               ← .site-header, .header-* classes
      footer.css               ← .site-footer, .footer-* classes
    sections/
      hero.css                 ← .hero-section, .hero-subtitle, .hero-device
      demo.css                 ← .demo-section, .demo-* classes
      multicam.css             ← .multicam-section, .multicam-device
      workflows.css            ← .workflows-section, .workflows-device
      pricing.css              ← .pricing-section, .pricing-device
```

## Adding New Styles

When adding a new section or component:
1. Create a new `.css` file in the appropriate directory (`sections/`, `layout/`, or top-level `styles/`)
2. Wrap all classes in `@layer components { ... }`
3. Add an `@import` for it in `src/index.css`
4. Use semantic class names that describe **what the element is**, not how it looks

```css
/* ✅ GOOD — src/styles/sections/testimonials.css */
@layer components {
  .testimonials-section { ... }
  .testimonial-card { ... }
  .testimonial-quote { ... }
}

/* ❌ BAD — inline utility soup in JSX */
<section className="flex flex-col gap-8 px-6 md:px-10 py-20 pointer-events-none">
```

## When to Use Inline Tailwind Utilities

Tailwind utility classes on JSX are fine for **simple one-off modifiers** that don't warrant a named class:

```tsx
// ✅ OK — single-purpose modifiers
<h1 className="type-display text-center">
<span className="block">

// ❌ BAD — multi-property layout belongs in a CSS file
<div className="flex flex-col lg:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-8 px-6 md:px-10">
```

Rule of thumb: if you're combining 3+ layout/spacing utilities, create a named class in CSS instead.

## Typography Scale

Defined as `@utility` blocks in `src/styles/typography.css`. Apply as single classes — they include family, size, weight, line-height, tracking, and colour:

| Class | Usage | Element |
|---|---|---|
| `type-display` | Hero heading | `<h1>` |
| `type-title` | Between-section title | `<h2>` |
| `type-subtitle` | Hero descriptor | `<p>` |
| `type-body` | Body copy, bullets | `<p>`, `<li>` |
| `type-card-heading` | Card/section sub-heading | `<h3>` |
| `para-gap` | Paragraph bottom spacing | Any text element |

## Design Tokens

Defined in `src/index.css` under `@theme`. Always use tokens rather than raw values:

| Token | Utility class | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-yellow` | `text-yellow`, `bg-yellow` | `#faff00` |
| `--color-pink` | `text-pink`, `bg-pink` | `#ff008c` |
| `--color-cyan` | `text-cyan` | `#2bffed` |
| `--color-purple` | `text-purple` | `#9b84ff` |
| `--color-magenta` | `text-magenta` | `#ff00bf` |
| `--color-bg` | `bg-bg` | `#000000` |
| `--color-border` | `border-border` | `rgba(255,255,255,0.18)` |
| `--font-heading` | `font-heading` | Hind |
| `--font-body` | `font-body` | Poppins |

## Pointer Events

The LiquidEther background sits at `z-index: 0`. Page content is at `z-index: 10`. Section containers use `pointer-events: none` so mouse events pass through to the background. Interactive elements (images, buttons, links) use `pointer-events: auto`.

This is handled in the CSS class definitions — you should not need to add these as inline Tailwind utilities.

## No Inline Style Objects

Do not use React `style={{ }}` props for layout. All layout goes in CSS files.
